{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","title":"lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2395,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-distance-finite]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","line":3886,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The Metric Is the Riemannian Distance]\n\\label{lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist}\n\n\\uses{thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces, def:riemannian-distance, prop:riemannian-distance-finite}\n\n\n\n\nFor the metric space of Theorem \\ref{thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces},\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}(p,q)=d_g(p,q).\n\\]\nThe right side from Definition \\ref{def:riemannian-distance} is real-valued by Proposition \\ref{prop:riemannian-distance-finite}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-distance,prop:riemannian-distance-finite}\n\\sketch The structure in Theorem \\ref{thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces} takes the finite real value of the extended distance from Definition \\ref{def:riemannian-distance}; finiteness is Proposition \\ref{prop:riemannian-distance-finite}. The identity is therefore definitional.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The Metric Is the Riemannian Distance] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d6d65747269632d73706163652d64697374\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23thm%3Ariemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces\">↗ thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-distance\">↗ def:riemannian-distance</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-distance-finite\">↗ prop:riemannian-distance-finite</a> <p></p>For the metric space of Theorem <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23thm%3Ariemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d6d616e69666f6c64732d6d65747269632d737061636573\">2</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\operatorname {dist}(p,q)=d_g(p,q).  \\]\">\\[  \\operatorname {dist}(p,q)=d_g(p,q).  \\]</span> The right side from Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-distance\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e6365\">15</a> is real-valued by Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-distance-finite\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-distance-finite\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d66696e697465\">15</a>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-distance\">↗ def:riemannian-distance</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-distance-finite\">↗ prop:riemannian-distance-finite</a> \\sketch The structure in Theorem <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23thm%3Ariemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7269656d616e6e69616e2d6d616e69666f6c64732d6d65747269632d737061636573\">2</a> takes the finite real value of the extended distance from Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-distance\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e6365\">15</a>; finiteness is Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ariemannian-distance-finite\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-distance-finite\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64697374616e63652d66696e697465\">15</a>. The identity is therefore definitional. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-distance-topology","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","title":"thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","label":"thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance","title":"def:riemannian-distance","label":"def:riemannian-distance"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-distance-finite","title":"prop:riemannian-distance-finite","label":"prop:riemannian-distance-finite"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","title":"lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[The Metric Is the Riemannian Distance]\n\\label{lem:riemannian-metric-space-dist}\n\n\\uses{thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces, def:riemannian-distance, prop:riemannian-distance-finite}\n\n\n\n\nFor the metric space of Theorem \\ref{thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces},\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}(p,q)=d_g(p,q).\n\\]\nThe right side from Definition \\ref{def:riemannian-distance} is real-valued by Proposition \\ref{prop:riemannian-distance-finite}.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-distance,prop:riemannian-distance-finite}\n\\sketch The structure in Theorem \\ref{thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces} takes the finite real value of the extended distance from Definition \\ref{def:riemannian-distance}; finiteness is Proposition \\ref{prop:riemannian-distance-finite}. The identity is therefore definitional.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","title":"thm:riemannian-manifolds-metric-spaces","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-distance","title":"def:riemannian-dist